*...+....1....+....2....+....3....+....4....+....5....+....6....+....7....+....8
TITLE
3 MeV isotropic photon point source at the centre of a 5 cm lead sphere
DEFAULTS                                                              PRECISIO
*
* Isotropic point source: BEAM WHAT(3) above 2000*pi mrad (10000.0) makes FLUKA
* emit over 4pi; BEAMPOS direction cosines are then ignored. No SOURCE routine.
BEAM          -0.003       0.0   10000.0       0.0       0.0       1.0PHOTON
BEAMPOS          0.0       0.0       0.0
*
GEOBEGIN                                                              COMBNAME
    0    0
RPP world      -100.0 +100.0 -100.0 +100.0 -100.0 +100.0
RPP fillbox     -50.0  +50.0  -50.0  +50.0  -50.0  +50.0
SPH leadsph       0.0    0.0    0.0    5.0
END
regBH        5 +world -fillbox
regFILL      5 +fillbox -leadsph
regLEAD      5 +leadsph
END
GEOEND
*
ASSIGNMA    BLCKHOLE     regBH
ASSIGNMA      VACUUM   regFILL
ASSIGNMA        LEAD   regLEAD
*
* Electron/positron and photon transport and production thresholds
EMFCUT       -1.0E-6    1.0E-6             regFILL  @LASTREG
EMFCUT       -1.0E-6    1.0E-6            BLCKHOLE  @LASTMAT          PROD-CUT
*
* Energy deposition on a mesh centred on the source (1 cm bins): the six
* half-spaces x<0, x>0, y<0, y>0, z<0, z>0 must agree for an isotropic source
USRBIN          10.0    ENERGY     -30.0       5.0       5.0       5.0EDEPSPH
USRBIN          -5.0      -5.0      -5.0      10.0      10.0      10.0&
*
* Track-length photon fluence in the lead: WHAT(5) = sphere volume 4/3*pi*5^3
USRTRACK        -1.0    PHOTON     -31.0   regLEAD   523.599     100.0TRKFLU
USRTRACK       0.003    1.0E-6                                        &
*
* Photon fluence escaping the sphere: WHAT(6) = sphere area 4*pi*5^2
USRBDX          99.0    PHOTON     -32.0   regLEAD   regFILL   314.159ESCAPE
USRBDX         0.003    1.0E-6     100.0                              &
*
RANDOMIZ         1.0    73519.
START        20000.0
STOP
